Selected packages only 8, not 9. Why? Base packages are kids, comedy, drama, scifi, games, news, movies, music = 8. Wait 71-140 ranges: kids 71-82 (12), comedy 83-88 (6), drama 89-94,96,105 (8), scifi 97-104 (8), games 106-110 (5), news 111-121 (11), movies 95,122-133,136 (14), music 134,135,137-140 (6). Sum 12+6+8+8+5+11+14+6 = 70. Yes 8 base packages, not 9. Good. Count 140.

Local detectGeo replaced with Des Moines content again. Channel 1 is Local Vault with Vantage Point senator; not local news. That's because no Des Moines newscast found. This is a real issue: user asked local news broadcasts; in Des Moines, the app shows a senator interview as "Local Vault". Could improve by ensuring channel 1 always uses a retro newscast fallback if no local news found, rather than local vault. The `buildLocalPlaylists` function sets `isVault` if no items for section. For news section, if no local news docs found, it becomes vault with spare docs. We could make channel 1 (news) fall back to the retro newscast pool (LOCAL_NEWS_FALLBACK) even when local city detection fails to find local news. This would satisfy the requirement. The current code already has `LOCAL_NEWS_ITEMS` and fallback. We can modify `detectGeo`:
- If local news items not found, ensure channel 1 uses fallback newscasts.
- Or modify `buildLocalPlaylists` for key "news" to use `LOCAL_NEWS_ITEMS` fallback items if itemsByKey.news is empty.

In `buildLocalPlaylists`, for Chicago it adds LOCAL_NEWS_ITEMS. For other cities, it only uses found items. We can add a generic fallback for news: if `itemsByKey.news` is empty, use `LOCAL_NEWS_ITEMS` values. That would give channel 1 actual retro newscasts (WBBM, WMAQ, WGN) even in Des Moines. But then "local" news is Chicago, not Des Moines. Still better than a senator interview? The user asked "find local news broadcasts ... Retro versions"; if no local city newscast exists, national retro newscasts are a reasonable fallback. The app's `LOCAL_NEWS_FALLBACK` already includes many city newscasts. We can use those.

Modify `buildLocalPlaylists`:
```
if (!itemsByKey.news || !itemsByKey.news.length) {
  itemsByKey.news = [];
  for (const [id,f] of Object.entries(LOCAL_NEWS_ITEMS)) { ... add ... }
  // plus fallback IDs with unknown duration? Need items with durations; only 3 known. Could use archive metadata fetch for fallback IDs.
}
```
